      "html": "<h4 id=\"heading-this-is-a-story-about-jeffery-hinton-a-very-renowned-scientist-who-is-also-known-as-the-father-of-ai-he-feels-regret-for-our-invention\">This is a story about Jeffery Hinton, a very renowned scientist who is also known as the father of AI he feels regret for our invention.</h4>\n<p>A few days ago, there was a lot of hype about ChatGPT, a language model created by OpenAI. However, recently, BBC News reported that the godfather of AI, Geoffrey Hinton, has left Google and warned of the dangers ahead. Since then, this news has spread everywhere. Let's try to understand the real reason behind this and explore the mystery behind it.</p>\n<p>He had been since 2013 until the end of April 2023. they were researching as usual when suddenly they realized that AI had become smarter than humans, which could now pose a threat to humans.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://cdn.hashnode.com/res/hashnode/image/upload/v1683924555158/0bf0f39e-316a-45f5-bc1b-bed136bfe2b7.gif\" alt class=\"image--center mx-auto\" /></p>\n<p>It made them feel a lot of regrets that they had created something that could potentially pose a threat to humanity in the future. This is one of those inventions that, after creating it, one could deeply regret as it could lead to the extinction of the entire human race. Other inventors also face concerns that in the future, an extraordinary AI may be developed that is so smart that it can train itself. Inventors of the atomic bomb, biological weapons, and jeans diffusion are also regretting their inventions in their lives.</p>",
